AB  - Traditional contracting processes often experience delays, miscommunication, and inefficiencies due to fragmented information and limited predictive capabilities. This paper proposes a framework to enhance transparency, accelerate decision-making, and optimize resource allocation throughout the contracting lifecycle. In this architecture, Legal-BERT (Bidirectional Encoder Representations from Transformers) extracts domain-specific semantic representations from legal documents, which are then processed by a Large Language Model for contextual reasoning and predictive analytics. Simultaneously, a Knowledge Graph organizes contractual entities into a structured relational map, enabling real-time query, compliance checks, and interpretability. The methodology combines Artificial Intelligence (AI) models for contract risk assessment with social network analysis to identify key influencers and streamline stakeholder engagement. The survey findings indicate that respondents expressed strong agreement (M=4.58, SD=1.23, and a 95% CI of [4.12, 5.04]) with the predictive analytics contributions of reduced negotiation time, improved compliance, and stronger relational governance. The paper offers practical implications for industries seeking agile and data-driven contracting solutions, supporting the emerging discourse on digital transformation in contract management.
