AB  - <p>This chapter examines the transformative impact of generative AI (GenAI) on the market, focusing on its innovative potential and operational challenges. It begins with an overview of GenAI fundamentals, including foundation models and their applications, and explores how organizations leverage these technologies to enhance productivity and address industry&#x2010;specific challenges. The discussion addresses practical considerations for data and AI professionals deploying GenAI, such as data quality, governance, and mitigating risks like hallucinations and bias. It underscores the need for a balanced approach that encourages experimentation while maintaining operational discipline. The historical context of GenAI is traced from early models like GANs and transformers to the breakthrough of large language models (LLMs) such as BERT and GPT&#x2010;3, culminating in the mainstream adoption of ChatGPT. The chapter also discusses the rapid pace of innovation and the flood of competitors that followed ChatGPT's release, as well as the unique characteristics of GenAI systems, which offer natural language interfaces and generate new content based on input. The role of foundation models, which are large, pretrained models capable of diverse downstream tasks, is also explored.</p>
