AB  - The most prevalent mental health issue in the world is anxiety disorders, which can be successfully treated with prompt intervention. PRISMA-based Overview: Anxiety Detection Research (2010–2026) It presents a detailed review and three big data modalities including physiological signals (ECg, EDA, Ppg), behavioral traits (speech, text, face) at various levels of psycho-physiological response and their multimodal detection. This review offers one of the first structured analyzes of modern architectural trends in affective computing from the self-reported neural data perspective, namely Transformer based models, Large Language Models (LLMs), and privacy preserved Federated Learning. The performance trend across datasets, feature extraction settings, and algorithmic frameworks that have been specifically designed or benchmarked for the purpose consistently point towards enhanced multimodal deep learning architectures. While these models improve prediction accuracy, they can also suffer from overfitting and the costs for implementation using actual wearables be more exhaustive in practice and increase computational cost.
